{#- Phone call and text bar, every page (art direction CB-a to CB-e, blueprint 3.10). Owner: WS2.
    Included once by layouts/v3.njk after the footer:  {% include "v3/sticky-bar.njk" %}

    Shown under 768px only (30-actions.css), position fixed at the bottom, ink-1 ground, 1px line
    hairline on top, 8px above and calc(8px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)) below a 56px control row,
    which is the height --scb reserves for scroll padding. Content is the action macro, slot "bar":
    the gold primary takes two thirds; the right third is the Text button while the shop is open and
    the plain "Calls open Tue 9 AM" words while it is not. data-bc-sticky is the container the script
    marks with data-state (open, closed, holiday, unknown). On /book (slug book, or the page variable
    on_book) the bar drops Request a time (it links to the page you are on) and Text until texts are
    confirmed, like the action macro's on_book option. data-test-clock is printed on every build
    except Netlify CONTEXT=production (lib/eleventy-ws2.js bcClockHook) and is what lets 30-actions.js
    honor the BC_NOW / ?bcnow= test clock. A production build never carries it. -#}
{%- from "v3/actions.njk" import action with context -%}
<div class="v3-bar" data-bc-sticky data-state="nojs" role="group" aria-label="{{ pages.shared.v3.actions.group_aria | safe }}"{% if bcClockHook %} data-test-clock{% endif %}>
  {{ action({ slot: "bar", service: "any", on_book: (slug == "book" or on_book) }) }}
</div>
